mt-mvcc-bench: rows_per_thread=1000 threads=[1, 8, 32, 64, 128] paired_rounds=11 bootstrap_reps=10000 synchronous=NORMAL wal_autocheckpoint=1000 available_parallelism=Some(64) apples_to_apples=false separate_tables=false transaction_granularity=one_bulk_transaction_per_worker
mt-mvcc-bench: NON-CITABLE: v7 binds the running executable, build/runtime source identity, Cargo.lock, invocation, toolchain, and measurement host to this same-invocation comparison, but bd-uh1fv still requires external watchdog, sanitized environment, matched retry/deadline semantics, external validation (and, when absent, capture) of a build-attested resolved dependency/feature-graph digest, counterbalanced topology receipts, immutable manifest, retained baseline history, and independent verification.
mt-mvcc-bench: settings contract: Both engines proved the listed effective PRAGMA values; equal names and readbacks do not establish cross-engine semantic equivalence.
mt-mvcc-bench: accounting contract: offered and committed writes share one row unit; attempted_writes counts physical INSERT calls; retried_operations records the existing engine-specific retry unit and is provenance only, not a cross-engine comparison metric.
mt-mvcc-bench: timing contract: workload_elapsed_ns begins only after every worker has opened and proved its effective settings, and ends at the last worker's transaction terminal point before connection teardown; worker_startup_elapsed_ns is reported separately.
